    {
      "value": "<p>Long Water&#39;s single large moon, a dark silicate body a third of Earth&#39;s radius, locked and airless. It is responsible for the twenty-six metre tides on the northern shelf and for the calendar that everyone on the world below shares. Its surface is heavily cratered and dusted with iron-rich fines, and it has been landed on four times, all by the Consortium.</p>",
